# Installed by PanelAlpha.
#
# OpenEMR serves from its own root, so sites/ is inside the document root.
# It holds:
#
#   sqlconf.php          the account's MySQL host, user and password
#   config.php           per-site settings
#   documents/           every uploaded patient document, generated PDF,
#                        EDI batch and remittance OpenEMR ever files
#   LBF/, letter_templates/, faxcache/
#
# The .php files execute rather than disclose themselves, and documents/ is
# empty on a fresh deploy -- which is exactly why this is easy to miss.
# Nothing otherwise stops `GET /sites/default/documents/<pid>/<file>` once the
# practice is in use, and on an electronic health record that is the whole
# ballgame.
#
# Upstream makes the same two cuts from the server config
# (docker/release/openemr.conf: `<Directory .../sites> AllowOverride None`
# plus a denied `<Directory .../sites/*/documents>`). A bind-mounted checkout
# cannot edit the vhost, so it is made here instead -- and made wider, because
# the deny below covers the whole tree rather than documents/ alone.
#
# sites/default/images/.htaccess re-opens the one part of this the application
# links to over HTTP: interface/globals.php builds practice and login logos as
# OE_SITE_WEBROOT . "/images/...". A deeper .htaccess's Require directives
# replace the parent's, which is what makes that work.
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order Allow,Deny
    Deny from all
</IfModule>
